# Patterns here use gitignore semantics, so a bare `timbot/` would match ANY
# directory of that name at any depth, including `assets/timbot/`, which is
# where the avatar lives. That shipped once and broke the image in production.
# Anchor every directory rule with a leading slash.

# Timbot source material. The grounding corpus, the recorded transcripts, and
# the evaluation set. Employment detail, unpublished context, and do-not-say
# rules that should never be fetchable at timlabarge.com/timbot/.
#
# The bot does not read these at runtime. `npm run timbot:build` compiles them
# into api/_lib/knowledge.js, which ships inside the serverless function bundle
# rather than as a static asset, so it is not publicly reachable either.
/timbot/

# Build tooling. Run locally, committed for provenance, never served.
/scripts/

# Raw avatar art and its notes. The processed webp beside them does ship.
/assets/timbot/timbot-avatar-source.webp
/assets/timbot/README.md
